GIMP Palette
Name: BattleGrid — Neon Netscape
Columns: 4
#
# Direction: you are inside the network, not looking at it. Everything glows
# from within against a violet void, and the duel reads at a glance because the
# two combatants own opposite ends of the colour wheel — cyan is yours, magenta
# is the intruder's, and nothing else in the game is allowed to be either.
#
# That is the whole design. A 3x3 grid gives the player almost no space to
# parse, so hue does the work that layout cannot: any cyan pixel is safe, any
# magenta pixel will hurt you, and the read survives being 3 tiles wide.
#
# amber-spark is the single exception and it is deliberately jarring — it only
# ever appears on the frame a hit lands, which is the one moment the player
# should not be reading hue at all.
#
 26  26  26	outline
 20  16  40	void-0-deep
 40  30  72	void-1
 66  50 112	void-2
100  84 156	void-3-rim
  0  88 112	cyan-0-shadow
  0 140 168	cyan-1
 46 196 224	cyan-2
150 240 255	cyan-3-hilite
104  16  76	magenta-0-shadow
168  32 116	magenta-1
228  72 160	magenta-2
255 160 214	magenta-3-hilite
 94  98 114	chrome-1
164 168 188	chrome-2
228 234 248	chrome-3-hilite
